{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-145979","model_call":32,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1022"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1022"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_664821645#2_1259363627","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1022","rank":4,"snippet":"\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_664821645#2_1259363627\" , \"end_char\": 3079.000000 , \"headings\": \"10 Self-Care Tips for Psychologists, Therapists, and Counselors 10 Self-Care Tips for Psychologists, Therapists, and <cover>Counselors This Article Contains: Mental Health and the Therapist Macro and Micro Self-Care Macro self-care Health care Taking a vacation Balance Treats Micro self-care 8 Strategies for Coping With Work Stress 1. Feeling love 2. Circle of care 3. Tea in a bubble 4. 4–7–8 Breath 5. Daily intention 6. Embrace yourself 7. Five senses 8. Reflection on impermanence PositivePsychology.com’s Resources A Take-Home Message References How useful was this article to you? About the Author Categories Legal Company Details Contact \" , \"segment\": \"Without adequate care, the mental health professional is equally at risk of “burnout, vicarious trauma, </cover>and compassion fatigue,” says Ashley Davis Bush (2015). And while the warning is stark, it is of genuine concern for anyone whose focus is others’ wellbeing. A report from 1990 found that nurses, therapists, social workers, and psychologists in psychiatric hospitals faced high occupational burnout "},"time":7},"model_calls":32,"document_judgments":30,"relevance_3":17,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
